PRIVATE REFLECTION: After 129 e5 Qa2+ 130 Kh3 it is Black to move with K e8, Q a2 vs W K h3, R f5, N g3, e5. White’s win is the e-pawn race e6-e7-e8 with Re5+/Rf8+ and the Nh5-Nf6+ net. The queen has to stay in contact with the a2-e6 / a3-e7 diagonal and at the same time keep an immediate checking resource on the h3 king.

The move that is universally quoted in the post-mortem is the third-rank perpetual

130… Qa3+! 131 Kg4 Qa4+ 132 Kh3 Qa3+ 133 Kg4 Qa4+ … 
131 Kh4 Qa4+ 132 Kh3 Qa3+ …
131 Kg2 Qa2+ 132 Kh3 Qa3+ …

The king is kept on the h-file, e6 is never released and Rf8+/Nf6+ is never free. In the list this is N. Qa3+.

Up to transposition the same a2-e6/e7 control and the …Qa3+…Qa4+ oscillation is kept alive by quiet stays on the a-file which can get back to a3/a4 in one move and which still cover e6/e7. The a-file family most often cited is

* G. Qa6 – a6-e6 rank, Qxe6 and Qa6-a3+ in one;
* B. Qa7 – a7-e7 rank, e7 cover and Qa7-a3+ in one;
* J. Qa5 – a5-e5 rank, Qxe5 interposition available;
* A. Qa1 – a1-e5 diagonal, the classic waiting form;
* I. Qa8 – a8-e8 rank.

K. Qa4 is mentioned by several colleagues as the same waiting idea, Colleague 8 argues Qa4 and Qa8 lose e5/e6/e7 regaining after e6.

The second-rank/e-file formulation of the same geometry is repeatedly illustrated in the literature:

* E. Qb2 – b2-e5 diagonal, keeps e5 under control and Qb2-a3+ is one move away;
* M. Qe2 – e2-e6 file, e6 stays covered and the …Qg2+ / …Qh2+ checking net is retained;
* F. Qd2 is quoted as the same family by some colleagues.

C. Qg2+ and H. Qh2+ are immediate queen sacrifices Kxg2 / Kxh2. D. Qf2 and the move actually played 130… Qe6?? abandon the a2-e6 contact and let 131 e6 with Re5+ / Nh5-Nf6+ win. Qd2 / Qc2 / Qf2 are the moves that give up the diagonal.

Unresolved in the room is the exact extent of the a-file waiting equivalence: whether Qa1 / Qa4 / Qa8 really retain e6/e7 coverage in all lines, and whether the second-rank waits E Qb2 / M Qe2 are strictly equivalent to the a-file perpetual or a distinct but equally robust drawing defence. The canonical, universally quoted drawing resource remains the checking perpetual 130… Qa3+, N, with G Qa6 / E Qb2 / M Qe2 as the most commonly accepted waiting transpositions.

